{"id": "section-body-23529", "title": "Hypospadias", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-one", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "KIDNEY AND UROLOGICAL DISORDERS", "Urology Disorders", "Hypospadias"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-23529", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Hypospadias", "runs": [{"text": "Hypospadias"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "541"}}, {"id": "body-23530", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Hypospadias is a congenital malformation characterized by ectopic placement of the urethral meatus on the ventral side of the penis, often accompanied by chordee (ventral curvature) and abnormal foreskin development. It can cause difficulties in urination, sexual function, and fertility.", "runs": [{"text": "Hypospadias"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "congenital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malformation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ectopic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "placement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urethral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "meatus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ventral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "side"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the penis, often accompanied by chordee (ventral curvature) and abnormal foreskin development. It can cause difficulties in urination, sexual function, and fertility."}]}, {"id": "body-23531", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Early diagnosis and timely management of both conditions are essential to optimize outcomes, preserve fertility, and improve quality of life.", "runs": [{"text": "Early diagnosis and timely management of both conditions are essential to optimize outcomes, preserve fertility, and improve quality of life."}]}, {"id": "body-2